  "note": "✋️ The node-graph gesture record (design §13.3 of ticket 26/09/30/NON-DESTRUCTIVE-HISTORY-EDITING): the ONE `nodeGraphEdit` row every node-graph host dispatches for a released node drag. Every `valid` row decodes to its `record` in Rust (`NodeDragRecord::from_row`) and TypeScript (`nodeDragRecordFromRow`), re-encodes to itself, satisfies the schema `$defs/NodeDragRow` under a third-party validator and `moves` as stated; every `invalid` row is refused by both decoders and by the schema. `commit` is the one-shot node-drag machine: the release of `gesture` by `actor` at `clock` under `tool` commits the leaves as ONE transaction with `id`.",
